      "content": "This argument strongly aligns with the \"Slippery Slope\" fallacy in political discourse, suggesting that a small, seemingly benign restriction will invariably lead to total control over thought. The core libertarian critique here is that the *power to define terms like \"truth\" or \"safety\" is the power to suppress dissent*, making the definition the real violation of free speech. Therefore, advocating for absolute freedom is based on the conviction that political power always corrupts the definition of acceptable discourse, regardless of the initial good intentions.",
